Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Test for Toptica DL pro laser divergence/beam defects with no optics \
modifications. Used thorlabs _______ and marked the top and right most edge, \
than turned dials till the marking reached opposite side and took \
measurements. Each dot had a radius of around .02\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \
put center of dot on edge, so each measurement has an uncertainty of around \
.02\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] from dot and .0005\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] from \
dials, so we will just say .02\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. The distance from the \
laser is measured from base of DL Pro aperture, the uncertainty increases as \
the bend of tape measure increase as it gets longer. 

The overall shape of the laser appears oval like with longest edges in \
horizontal/x direction (at first). over distance this actually switches to \
the longest being vertical/z direction. This is based on the brightest point \
of laser seen on camera, but only the brightest part is what we can see \
visually not using my iPhone 14 camera 1x zoom, each picture was taken from 8 \
1/2\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] away. Look bellow to see. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.932473116107666*^9, 3.9324731479943657`*^9}, {
  3.932473296535942*^9, 3.9324735870131063`*^9}, {3.9324737191578026`*^9, 
  3.9324737197028666`*^9}, {3.9324738274125085`*^9, 3.932473831872323*^9}, {
  3.932474137110506*^9, 
  3.932474142057374*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2e005d2c-264b-4544-9238-\
94c88d353df4"],

